==English==

===Etymology===
[[char]] + [[woman]].

===Noun===
{{en-noun|char|women}}

# {{chiefly|British}} A woman employed to do [[housework]].

Note: In the nineteenth century, the charlady worked for weekly wages and usually came and went on a daily basis.

====Synonyms====
*[[cinderella]]
*[[cleaning woman]]

